  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kenya Inter-Religious Lobby Campaign for Debt Relief Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.The Government of Kenya takes immediate steps to drastically reduce the domestic debt stock and to work for a reduction or cancellation of the international debt.
2.Parliament creates legislation to establish monitoring mechanisms that guarantee the official approval of new loans by Parliament on behalf of the Kenyan people and that facilitate the transparent use of development funds.
3.The content of the Public Debt Register will be published and open to public scrutiny.
4.The Government of Kenya takes action against those persons who have siphoned-off international loans into private accounts and to recover the monies lost.</narrative>
  </description>
